The .claude/commands/*.md files were carried over from another repo and called
six helper scripts that have never existed here: beads-context.sh,
conflict-detect.sh, dep-guard.sh, pr-coordinator.sh, smart-status.sh and
validate.sh. Every one of those invocations was an instruction the agent could
not carry out.

Rather than port ~4k lines of shell, each call site now says what to actually
do in this repo, matching how docs/agents/forge-workflow.md was already
de-scripted:

- beads-context.sh (stage transitions, progress, design/acceptance metadata)
  -> forge issue comment / forge issue show, re-read to confirm it landed.
  Beads is retired; the kernel is the issue authority.
- smart-status.sh -> read the real state: forge ready, git status -sb,
  git worktree list, gh pr list.
- pr-coordinator.sh merge-sim -> git merge-tree --write-tree against
  origin/HEAD, which is what the simulation was approximating.
  merge-order / auto-label / stale-worktrees dropped: they coordinate a
  multi-PR queue this solo app does not have.
- conflict-detect.sh and dep-guard.sh -> dropped. Both exist to arbitrate
  between concurrent developers over shared contracts; ScoreEasy has one
  developer. What survives is the part that still bites: your own parallel
  worktrees and open PRs.

Every command written here was verified to exist before being written --
forge/gh subcommands against --help and live runs, git merge-tree flags
against git 2.51, package.json scripts against the file. `git grep` for the
six script names now returns nothing, and every scripts/ path still
referenced in .claude/commands resolves on disk.

Closes e6e95c70

